        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the number of tricks bid, or prevent the declarer from making their bid. First to 51 points wins the game.',
          gameplay: 'The declarer leads to the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible. If unable to follow, may play any card. Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit if no trumps.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if able',
            'Meksiko bid: win all 10 tricks, no talon, no trumps',
            'Declarer takes talon (except in Meksiko) and chooses trumps',
            'Discarded talon cards count as won tricks for declarer',
            'First to 51 points wins',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Only bid what you think you can make. Count your high cards and consider the talon's potential. In defense, try to force the declarer to use trumps early.",
          intermediate: "The talon exchange is crucial - discard cards that don't help your contract. Watch opponents' play to deduce their holdings. Coordinate with the other defender to stop the declarer.",
          advanced: 'Card counting is essential. Track all trumps and high cards. Bluff in bidding to push opponents into difficult contracts. The Meksiko bid requires perfect hand evaluation.',
          tips: [
            "Don't overbid - failing a contract gives opponents significant points",
            'Save your highest trumps for critical tricks',
            'If defending, try to make the declarer guess which defender has which cards',
            'The Meksiko bid should only be attempted with an exceptional hand',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
